abstract: >-
  Code, pre-registrations, provenance manifests, and evaluation artifacts for
  an HSTU-style pure-PyTorch sequential recommender on the Amazon Reviews 2023
  5-core benchmark: a strictly causal, zero-initialized FIR temporal filter
  (positive on all four categories tested; two under a dedicated
  pre-registration), two counted pre-registered per-category point-estimate
  comparisons against published single-run HSTU-BLaIR values
  (Musical_Instruments; Office_Products under the redesigned V3
  pre-registration with an environment-matched reference — the earlier V1
  campaign remains VOID by its own tripwire), a dataset-conditional long-tail
  pattern with thinning interventions, a fail-closed artifact-graph build that
  recomputes every printed number from source artifacts, and a shim harness
  that executes the reference comparator implementation locally. No SOTA claim
  of any kind; no paired or distributional superiority over single-run
  comparators.
